---
/**
 * Event submission from the hub, routed to the right town.
 *
 * Someone who lands on insidethetowns.com with an event to tell us about
 * should not have to work out which of seven sites owns it. But each town
 * posts to its own endpoint, so the form has to know where to send a
 * submission before it sends one.
 *
 * Rather than keep a second copy of the town form in sync, this page is a
 * chooser: pick the town, go to that town's form. One form to maintain, and
 * no way for a hub submission to land in the wrong town's inbox — which is
 * the failure a duplicated form invites and nobody would notice for weeks.
 *
 * The picker is a plain link list, so it works without JavaScript. The select
 * above it is a convenience for long lists, not the mechanism.
 */
import Page from '@/layouts/Page.astro';
import { countyLabel, getHub, liveTowns } from '@/config';

const hub = getHub();
const towns = liveTowns();
const mailto = `mailto:${hub.social.email}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('Event submission')}`;
---
<Page
  title="Submit an event"
  eyebrow="Inside the Towns"
  description="Tell us about an event in any of the towns we cover. Listings are free."
  intro={`Anything open to the public in ${towns.length} Front Range towns. Listings are free — nobody pays to be listed and nobody can pay to be higher up.`}
  narrow
>
  <p class="text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed">
    Which town is it in? Each guide has its own form, so this takes you to the right one.
  </p>

  <ul class="mt-7 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2" data-town-picker>
    {towns.map((town) => (
      <li>
        <a
          href={`https://${town.domain}/submit-event/`}
          class="group flex items-baseline justify-between gap-3 rounded-lg bg-raised px-5 py-4 no-underline ring-1 ring-line-soft transition hover:ring-accent-line"
        >
          <span class="font-medium group-hover:text-accent-text">{town.name}</span>
          <span class="text-sm text-ink-faint">{countyLabel(town)}</span>
        </a>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <div class="prose mt-14">
    <h2>Not one of those towns?</h2>
    <p>
      We cover {towns.length} so far and add more when there is somebody to keep a guide current. If your event is
      somewhere else on the northern Front Range, <a href={mailto}>send it to us anyway</a> — it tells us where to go
      next, which is worth knowing.
    </p>

    <h2>What happens to it</h2>
    <p>
      Every submission is checked against the organizer’s own page before it goes up, usually within a couple of days.
      That is why the form asks for a link. Nothing is published that we could not verify, and nothing is charged for
      — see the <a href="/editorial/">editorial policy</a> for why that matters.
    </p>
  </div>
</Page>
